 "result": "fibmod.py is a fast-doubling Fibonacci mod 1e9+7. It walks the bits of n from the top, keeping (F(k), F(k+1)) and reducing mod once per step. It reads all of stdin, splits on whitespace, and writes one result per line. The adopted variant scored 2.751 against a 2.585 baseline, a +6% win. It matches all sample outputs in the public fibmod kit. Further gains would need more than 3% beyond this, and the remaining ideas (batching or caching across inputs) are unlikely to clear that bar, so I am resting here.",
